@startuml view-3
title View 3 - Reservation lifecycle (State pattern) and rules tied to it
[*] --> ACTIVE : makeReservation (UC7)
ACTIVE --> CANCELLED : cancel (UC9)\nrule: owner only, >= 6h before slot start
ACTIVE --> CONFIRMED : check-in (UC10)\nrule: same day, <= 10 min after start
ACTIVE --> EXPIRED : manageEnd (UC16, scheduler)\nstart + 10 min passed, no check-in
CONFIRMED --> COMPLETED : manageEnd (UC16)\nslot end passed
CANCELLED --> CANCELLED : forceCancel when room deleted\n(StudyRoomManager.deleteStudyRoom)
note right of ACTIVE
ACTIVE and CONFIRMED occupy the seat
(ReservationRegistry.occupiesSlot):
used by Seat.isAvailable, uniqueness rule,
room monitoring and statistics.
end note
note bottom
Every setState() notifies observers (NotificationManager -> email).
ConfirmedState cancel/checkIn return false.
end note
@enduml
